<title>NETHERLANDS: SOCCER-NETHERLANDS BEAT SAN MARINO 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-NETHERLANDS BEAT SAN MARINO 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Netherlands beat San Marino</p>
<p>4-0 (halftime 1-0) in their World Cup European group seven</p>
<p>qualifier on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Patrick Kluivert 44, Frank de Boer 58, 93, Pierre</p>
<p>van Hooijdonk 82</p>
<p>Attendance: 48,000</p>
<p>Group seven standings:</p>
<p>		     P   W   D   L   F   A  Pts</p>
<p> Netherlands     4   4   0   0  17   2  12</p>
<p> Belgium	   4   3   0   1   7   5   9</p>
<p> Wales	     6   2   1   3  14  12   7</p>
<p> Turkey	    3   1   1   1   8   2   4</p>
<p> San Marino	5   0   0   5   0  25   0</p>
<p>Teams: Netherlands -- 1-Edwin van der Sar, 2-Michael</p>
<p>Reiziger, 4-Frank de Boer, 3-Jaap Stam, 5-Arthur Numan, 7-Aron</p>
<p>Winter (Marc Overmars 33), 6-Wim Jonk (Richard Witschge 73),</p>
<p>10-Clarence Seedorf (Pierre van Hooijdonk 73), 11-Phillip Cocu,</p>
<p>9-Patrick Kluivert, 8-Dennis Bergkamp</p>
<p>San Marino -- 1-Federico Gasperoni, 4-Luca Gobbi (Vittorio</p>
<p>Valentini 64), 3-Damiano Vanucci (Mirko Gennari 78), 2-Mauro</p>
<p>Valentini, 6-Ivan Matteoni, 5-William Guerra, 7-Riccardo</p>
<p>Muccioli, 8-Marco Mazza, 9-Paolo Montagna (Nicola Bacciocchi</p>
<p>81), 10-Fabio Francini, 11-Bryan Gasperoni.</p>
<p>Remaining matches:</p>
<p> Apr  2	 - Turkey	v Netherlands</p>
<p> Apr 30	 - San Marino  v Netherlands</p>
<p> Apr 30	 - Turkey	v Belgium</p>
<p> June 7	 - Belgium     v San Marino</p>
<p> Aug 20	 - Turkey	v Wales</p>
<p> Sep  6	 - Netherlands v Belgium</p>
<p> Sep 10	 - San Marino  v Turkey</p>
<p> Oct 11	 - Netherlands v Turkey</p>
<p> Oct 11	 - Belgium     v Wales</p>
</text>
